{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DobQa2mXRR8ApKbdYCahks","type":"tool_result","content":"VENUE.md\nclaims_grounding.json\nclosed_form_gap.json\ndraft_reference_gaps_agent_claude_20261027_173512.log\ndraft_reference_gaps_prompt.md\nfigure_manifest.json\nfigures\nglobal_memory\nglobal_memory_recent.json\nglobal_memory_summary.md\nmemory.md\npaper.bst\npaper.pdf\npaper.sty\npaper.tex\npaper_agent_claude_20261027_173512.log\npaper_data.json\npaper_diagnostics\npaper_diagnostics_20261027_173512_4043.log\npaper_events_20261027_173512.jsonl\npaper_prep_20261027_173512.json\npaper_prompt.md\npaper_strategy.json\npaper_strategy.md\npaper_strategy_agent_claude_20261027_173512.log\npaper_strategy_prompt.md\npaper_strategy_resolution.json\nprotocol_facts.json\nprotocol_inputs\nreference_query_plan.json\nreference_query_plan.md\nreference_query_plan_agent_claude_20261027_173512.log\nreference_query_plan_prompt.md\nreference_query_plan_validation_feedback.json\nreference_query_plan_validation_feedback.md\nreference_retrieval.log\nreferences.bib\nreferences_provenance.json\nresults\nscientific-evidence\nscripts\nsource_evidence\nstrategy_validation_feedback.json\nstrategy_validation_feedback.md\ntask\n38013 paper.tex\n  922 references.bib\n38935 total\n# Global Memory Summary\n\nUse as qualitative context only; do not use as quantitative grounding source.\n\n## Recent Entries\n\n- 2026-10-27T00:00:00Z | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Selected resistance-calibrated Matthews predictor for cover time; alternatives: pure simple-stat regression, exact subset DP. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=no experimental evidence yet.\n  - evidence: No execution during idea generation; motivated by Matthews bound and commute-time identity.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n{\n  \"status\": \"ready\",\n  \"selected_prompt_family\": \"paper_standalone\",\n  \"recommended_title\": \"How Far Can Five Cheap Graph Statistics Go? Log-Linear Cover-Time Prediction on Small Connected Graphs\",\n  \"central_question\": \"For connected graphs with 6<=n<=30, does a ridge model on a handful of cheap graph statistics (n, m, mean degree, max degree, diameter) predict Monte Carlo start-averaged random-walk cover time with lower family-macro log error than the generic 2m(n-1) bound?\",\n  \"central_thesis\": \"On the sealed held-out graphs, a five-statistic log-linear ridge predictor (family-macro log MAE 0.181) is far closer to Monte Carlo cover times than the 2m(n-1) bound (1.754) and than constant and label-shuffled controls (0.870, 1.423), with median Monte Carlo relative SE about 0.029; this is measured only on 12 synthetic families, 24 test graphs, and the question of which families it fails on is not answered by the retained evidence.\",\n  \"narrative_rationale\": \"The only grounded, completed evidence is the sealed final evaluation (outcome qualified, status completed) of the frozen selection, which is the seed baseline ridge predictor (study.selection_kind=baseline; investigation completed_no_winner; 1 attempt, 0 scored, 1 unscored; search score delta 0.0). The strongest honest story is therefore a calibrated, narrow empirical-measurement paper: a cheap-statistic log-linear predictor versus the worst-case bound and sanity controls, with explicit scope limits. No improvement over a baseline is claimed because the studied method IS the baseline; the unscored resistance/Matthews variant has no performance evidence and is not a result. The second half of the research question (error vs graph type) cannot be answered quantitatively because per-family metrics are absent from paper_data; the paper must say so (unknown, not a failure) and use the family design only as a description of the test distribution and as a stated limitation/future-work item.\",\n  \"prior_paper_story_status\": \"preserved\",\n  \"edit_framing_decision\": \"Not edit mode: no previous_paper or staged inputs exist (edit-context placeholders are unfilled), so there is no prior story to preserve or replace; field value is nominal. Fresh thesis-first framing chosen over a Matthews/resistance-predictor story, which lacks any scored evidence.\",\n  \"staged_input_impact\": [\n    \"No staged paper, program, or result inputs were provided; framing is based solely on paper_data.json final_evaluation and downstream_study.\"\n  ],\n  \"method_groups\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Five-statistic log-linear ridge predictor (frozen selection)\",\n      \"role\": \"proposed\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"This is the studied method (frozen selection = seed baseline program): standardized log n, log m, log mean degree, log max degree, log diameter; ridge (lambda=1, unpenalised intercept) on log cover time, fit in-episode on labelled training graphs; exact method visible in source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Generic 2m(n-1) worst-case bound\",\n      \"role\": \"baseline\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"The comparator named in the research question (Aleliunas et al.); final bound macro log MAE 1.754. Also the fallback when no training data is supplied.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Constant predictor control\",\n      \"role\": \"baseline\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Family-agnostic sanity control (0.870); shows the gain is not just calibrating the overall scale.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Label-shuffled control\",\n      \"role\": \"ablation\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"Negative control (1.423) showing the ridge fit uses the statistic-to-target relation rather than fitting artefacts. Describe only as the evaluator's shuffled-label control; do not invent finer feature ablations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Relabeling-invariance check\",\n      \"role\": \"supporting\",\n      \"include_reason\": \"perm_max_rel_dev=0.0 documents that predictions depend only on relabeling-invariant statistics (validity check, not a performance claim).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"results_focus\": [\n    \"Single direct comparison of family-macro log MAE (sealed final): ridge 0.181 vs constant 0.870, shuffled 1.423, 2m(n-1) bound 1.754; improvement_vs_bound 1.572 (consistent with 1.754-0.181).\",\n    \"Monte Carlo uncertainty: median relative SE of labels ~0.029 (log-scale ~0.03 order), much smaller than the 0.181 model error, so label noise is a minor part of the measured error; present as a noise-floor context, not as a confidence interval on the model score.\",\n    \"Episode variability: 3 seeded episodes (201-203) all gave identical score -0.18137 (deterministic candidate, fixed test graphs/labels) so episode-to-episode spread is zero and must NOT be presented as sampling uncertainty over graphs; state that uncertainty over graph draws was not measured.\",\n    \"Qualification: outcome qualified, status completed, correct=true (final.qualification.*); candidate_diagnostics_trust is 'unverified' - disclose. No failed gates to discuss; do not claim validity beyond the reported qualification.\",\n    \"Scope and unknowns: per-family errors, per-size errors, and which families the predictor fails on are NOT available; write as an explicit open item. Describe the test set composition (12 families, 2 test graphs each, 24 total; 36 final train graphs, 3 per family) only if drawn from the task evaluator/resources and phrase as design description.\",\n    \"Search vs final separation: search baseline score -0.1913 (delta 0.0, 0 of 1 attempts scored) is a different evaluation scope from final -0.1814; do not compare them as an improvement. Unscored attempt = missing evidence.\"\n  ],\n  \"figure_plan\": [\n    \"Fig 1 (overview, early, page 1-2): concept schematic of the pipeline - graph from a family -> five cheap statistics -> ridge on log cover time -> prediction compared to Monte Carlo label, against the 2m(n-1) bound, with the family-macro log-error aggregation hierarchy.\",\n    \"Fig 2 (main result): bar chart of family-macro log MAE for the four predictors (ridge, constant, shuffled, 2m(n-1) bound) with annotation of the Monte Carlo median relative SE as context; no error bars unless grounded (none are).\"\n  ],\n  \"figure_specs\": [\n    {\n      \"figure_id\": \"overview_pipeline\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"purpose\": \"Glance-value summary of the studied object: statistics-only predictor vs worst-case bound, MC ground truth, and evaluation aggregation (graph -> family mean -> family macro mean -> episode mean).\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"diagram\",\n      \"preferred_generator\": \"generate-concept-figure\",\n      \"group_by\": \"pipeline_stage\",\n      \"metric\": \"none\",","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7f1591f-7233-402d-8404-9d3c6c7aef39","uuid":"4eb746c7-cf45-4e91-a3af-a5720a8e5e2d","timestamp":"2026-10-27T17:47:45.076Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"VENUE.md\nclaims_grounding.json\nclosed_form_gap.json\ndraft_reference_gaps_agent_claude_20261027_173512.log\ndraft_reference_gaps_prompt.md\nfigure_manifest.json\nfigures\nglobal_memory\nglobal_memory_recent.json\nglobal_memory_summary.md\nmemory.md\npaper.bst\npaper.pdf\npaper.sty\npaper.tex\npaper_agent_claude_20261027_173512.log\npaper_data.json\npaper_diagnostics\npaper_diagnostics_20261027_173512_4043.log\npaper_events_20261027_173512.jsonl\npaper_prep_20261027_173512.json\npaper_prompt.md\npaper_strategy.json\npaper_strategy.md\npaper_strategy_agent_claude_20261027_173512.log\npaper_strategy_prompt.md\npaper_strategy_resolution.json\nprotocol_facts.json\nprotocol_inputs\nreference_query_plan.json\nreference_query_plan.md\nreference_query_plan_agent_claude_20261027_173512.log\nreference_query_plan_prompt.md\nreference_query_plan_validation_feedback.json\nreference_query_plan_validation_feedback.md\nreference_retrieval.log\nreferences.bib\nreferences_provenance.json\nresults\nscientific-evidence\nscripts\n